Vipraah - All Brahmins; Satya - True; Ashishah - Whose blessings; Tushtaah - Being extremely pleased; Shraddhaaya - With reverence; Labdha-Dakshinaah - Receiving Dakshina; Ashishah - Blessings; Yuyujuh - Giving; Kshatrah - O Vidura;
Adi-Rajayah - To the first king; Sat-Krutah - Being honored. Adiraj Pruthu, with utmost respect, offered all kinds of gifts to all the Brahmins present at that Yagya. These Brahmins, pleased, gave the king their heartfelt blessings. By you, O mighty-armed one, all are gathered. Worshipped by the gods, charitable, and the best of the gods. 42. Meaning of the word

By you—by you; Aahuta—invited; Maha-baho—He is the most powerful; Sarve—all; Eva—certainly; Samagataha—together;
Worshipped—honored; Daan—by donation; Manabhyam—with respect; Pitra—dwellers of the fatherland; Deva—deities; Rishi—group of sages;
Humans—as well as ordinary people. All the sages and Brahmins said: O mighty king, at your invitation, all classes of beings have participated in this assembly.
They have come from the world of ancestors and the world of heaven, as well as
common people and sages have also attended this assembly. Now they are all very pleased with your behavior and
your donation. Thus, under the fourth canto of Srimad Bhagavatam, the "King Prithu's hundred Ashwamedha Yagya" named
The twenty-ninth chapter's Bhakti Vedanta meaning is completed.
